message.content:
Artificial flower wreaths of plastic fall under heading 6702: "Artificial flowers, foliage and fruit and parts thereof; articles made of artificial flowers, foliage or fruit." Subheading 6702.10 covers plastic articles. Under 6702.10.20 are "Christmas decorations" and 6702.10.40 "Other"? Checking the actual structure: 6702.10.20 is for "Wreaths, garlands... " hmm. The HTSUS for 6702.10 reads "Of plastics": 6702.10.20 "Flowers, foliage and fruit, and parts thereof; articles made of artificial flowers, foliage or fruit: Christmas ornaments"? I recall 6702.10.20 is "Christmas tree decorations"? Actually I recall 6702.10.20 "Wreaths, garlands and similar articles"? Hmm: CBP rulings for plastic artificial wreaths cite 6702.10.4000 (Other). Rulings on artificial wreaths with plastic flowers cite 6702.10.4000 with a 25% rate, and ones for Christmas wreaths cite 6702.10.2000. This is a flower wreath, not Christmas, so 6702.10.40.00.

The base is toad vine (natural material), but the plastic flowers give the wreath its essential character, so it is classified as plastic.

{"hts_code": "6702.10.4000", "reason": "Wreaths of artificial plastic flowers with a mostly hidden natural vine base are articles made of artificial flowers of plastics under heading 6702, not Christmas-specific, so they fall in subheading 6702.10.40."}
